### 5.3.5 Error Handling

**Code Evidence - Graceful Error Handling:**

```typescript
// Graceful error handling throughout
try {
  const tx = await contract.batchVote(votes);
  await tx.wait();
} catch (error) {
  if (error.code === "ACTION_REJECTED") {
    toast.error("Transaction rejected by user");
  } else if (error.message.includes("Already voted")) {
    toast.error("You have already voted in this category");
  } else {
    toast.error("Transaction failed. Please try again.");
  }
}
```

### 5.3.6 Connection Pooling

**Code Evidence - Database Connection Pool:**

```typescript
// File: server/src/db.ts
const pool = new Pool({
  host: process.env.DB_HOST,
  port: parseInt(process.env.DB_PORT || "5432"),
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
  user: process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,
  max: 20, // Connection pool for high availability
  idleTimeoutMillis: 30000,
  connectionTimeoutMillis: 2000,
});
```

### 5.3.7 System Reset Capability

**Code Evidence - System Reset:**

```solidity
// File: src/contracts/VotingSystem.sol (Lines 227-242)
// Prepare for next election without redeployment
function resetSystem() external onlyAdmin {
    require(currentElection.state == ElectionState.Ended);
    _resetAllVoters();
    _resetAllCandidates();
    _resetAllCategories();
    delete currentElection;
}
```

