# 6. Objective 4 Achievement (Evaluation)

**Objective:** To evaluate the system for security, performance and usability in simulation of controlled election environments checking the reliability of practical implementation.

---

## 6.1 Security Evaluation

### 6.1.1 Security Testing Performed

_Table 27: Security Testing Results_

| Test Category              | Before           | After                | Improvement      |
| -------------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------- | ---------------- |
| Snyk Security Scan         | 35% (21 issues)  | 65% (11 issues)      | +30% improvement |
| Hardcoded Secrets          | Present          | Removed              | ✅ Fixed         |
| X-Powered-By Header        | Enabled          | Disabled             | ✅ Fixed         |
| Database Password Security | Default fallback | Required env var     | ✅ Fixed         |
| Admin Credentials          | Hardcoded        | Environment variable | ✅ Fixed         |

**Evidence:** `SECURITY_SETUP.md` (5,990 bytes)

### 6.1.2 Smart Contract Security

_Table 28: Smart Contract Security Features_

| Feature               | Implementation                      | Purpose                     |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Access Control        | `onlyAdmin` modifier                | Restrict admin functions    |
| State Validation      | `electionActive` modifier           | Ensure valid election state |
| Reentrancy Protection | State changes before external calls | Prevent reentrancy attacks  |
| Input Validation      | `require` statements                | Validate all inputs         |

**Code Evidence - Access Control:**

```solidity
// File: src/contracts/VotingSystem.sol (Lines 101-104)
modifier onlyAdmin() {
    require(msg.sender == admin, "Only admin");
    _;
}
```

**Code Evidence - State Validation:**

```solidity
// File: src/contracts/VotingSystem.sol (Lines 121-127)
modifier electionActive() {
    _checkAndUpdateElectionState();
    require(currentElection.state == ElectionState.Active);
    require(block.timestamp >= currentElection.startTime);
    require(block.timestamp <= currentElection.endTime);
    _;
}
```

### 6.1.3 Authentication Security

_Table 29: Authentication Security Features_

| Feature           | Implementation        | Details              |
| ----------------- | --------------------- | -------------------- |
| JWT Tokens        | Session-based auth    | 24h expiry           |
| OTP Verification  | 6-digit code          | 10-minute expiry     |
| OTP Attempt Limit | Maximum 5 attempts    | Prevents brute force |
| Resend Cooldown   | 60-second delay       | Prevents spam        |
| Wallet Signature  | MetaMask verification | Cryptographic proof  |

### 6.1.4 Input Validation

_Table 30: Input Validation Layers_

| Layer          | Technology             | Implementation      |
| -------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------- |
| Frontend       | React Hook Form + Zod  | Schema validation   |
| Backend        | express-validator      | Request validation  |
| Database       | PostgreSQL constraints | Data integrity      |
| Smart Contract | Solidity require       | On-chain validation |

