| Database Queries         | < 100ms | ✅ Yes   | Pass   |
| Zero Server Crashes      | 100%    | ✅ Yes   | Pass   |

### 6.2.3 Performance Optimizations

_Table 33: Performance Optimization Techniques_

| Optimization       | Implementation                        | Benefit                  |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
| Batch Voting       | Single transaction for multiple votes | Lower gas costs          |
| Connection Pooling | Max 20 concurrent connections         | High availability        |
| Efficient Queries  | Single call returns all data          | Reduced network overhead |
| Caching            | LocalStorage for session data         | Faster page loads        |

**Code Evidence - Batch Voting:**

```solidity
// File: src/contracts/VotingSystem.sol (Lines 450-489)
// Gas optimization
function batchVote(VoteChoice[] memory votes) external {
    // Single transaction for multiple votes
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < votes.length; i++) {
        // Process all votes in one transaction
    }
}
```

**Code Evidence - Connection Pooling:**

```typescript
// File: server/src/db.ts
max: 20,  // 20 concurrent connections
idleTimeoutMillis: 30000,
connectionTimeoutMillis: 2000
```

**Code Evidence - Efficient Queries:**

```solidity
// File: src/contracts/VotingSystem.sol (Lines 391-425)
// Single call returns all data
function getCandidatesForCategory(uint256 categoryId)
    returns (
        uint256[] memory ids,
        string[] memory names,
        string[] memory parties,
        uint256[] memory votes
    )
```

